From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:57:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpu compositor: the card's scroll applied in the compositor,
 the engine scrolled only when it leaves the displayport; two-band reads

T-502 (2026-10-18). Without APZ a scroll was a main-thread scroll: every step repainted the
newly exposed strip and re-uploaded the content layer, 12-17 fps on a scripted pan. Now the
daemon sends the card's scroll (CSS px, absolute) through jihad_offscreen_set_scroll, and
AsyncCompositionManager applies the difference to the engine's own scroll (the metrics' offset)
as an async transform on the root scroll frame's content, the way APZ would, with
AlignFixedAndStickyLayers keeping fixed and sticky layers still. The daemon moves the engine's
scroll only when the card's scroll nears the edge of the displayport painted around the last
anchor.

The frame request carries two bands and a row shift: on a frame whose only change is the
scroll (no composite request since the last composite: no transaction, no animation step; the
layer diff cannot tell, the async transform is a shadow transform and the diff reports the
content's whole bounds), the diff is dropped, the destination's rows are moved by the shift on
the compositor thread, and only the bands asked for (what entered, the rows fixed and sticky
layers cover, which the bridge reports after each composite) are composed and read.
